# Decisions

Record choices that later agents should not silently reverse. Newest first. Full ADRs live in `docs/DECISIONS.md` after Phase 0.

## 2026-10-24 — Phase 3 RPG

- **Decision (D-024):** Persist rolled `max_hp` / `max_mp` on `CharacterRecord`. Base stats + AP/SP only; derive the rest.
- **Decision (D-025):** LOCAL debug `/advance <class>` skips job reqs and grants 5 AP / 6 SP so class skills are playable before Phase 7.
- **Decision (D-022 still):** Novice `base_weapon_attack` **140** — still ~3 hits per Puddlet.
- **Revisit when:** Phase 4 loot or Phase 7 job NPC.

## 2026-10-24 — Novice weapon attack 80

- **Decision (D-022):** `stats.json` `base_weapon_attack` **140**, `mob_skill_attack` **12** (play-test retune). Attack keys are J / X / left-click, not Ctrl (D-023).
- **Why:** Phase 2 requires data-driven damage without hard-coded swing numbers.
- **Revisit when:** Play-test or Phase 3 AP/class pass.

## 2026-10-24 — Movement feel v1 / default map

- **Decision (D-020):** Default `CharacterRecord` map is `map_test_movement`.
- **Decision (D-021):** Movement tunables live in `data/stats.json` (walk 125, jump -330, gravity 1000, climb 80).
- **Why:** Phase 1 play-test boots the yard; designers tweak feel in JSON.
- **Revisit when:** Town maps (Phase 5) or a feel pass after play-test.

## 2026-10-17 — Canonical GitHub repo

- **Decision (D-019):** The project lives at https://github.com/icors2/Action-Story. `origin` points there. Issues, PRs, Actions, and releases use this repo — not Cursor_Forge.
- **Why:** Owner designated Action-Story as the product repository. Cursor_Forge was the starter template.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Keep developing on Cursor_Forge; a new private repo.
- **Revisit when:** The public name/brand changes (codename is still Skyrope).

## 2026-10-17 — Skyrope bootstrap

- **Decision (D-017):** Pin Godot `4.7.2-stable` in `.godot-version`. Typed `Dictionary[K, V]` is allowed.
- **Why:** Latest stable as of 2026-10-17. 4.8 is still beta. BUILD_SCOPE §8.2 forbade typed dicts unless the pin supports them and the log approves it.
- **Alternatives rejected:** 4.3 (spec minimum); 4.4.1 (stale example in spec); 4.8-beta1.
- **Revisit when:** Next Godot minor, only between milestones on a branch with the full suite.

- **Decision:** Enable only Context7 and GitHub MCP.
- **Why:** Godot/FastAPI docs + issues/PRs. No web deploy, hosted Postgres, or payments in this stack.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Enabling the whole catalog; Neon/Supabase (homelab Postgres); Vercel/Render.
- **Revisit when:** A later phase needs another tool the agents will actually call.

- **Decision (D-001–D-016):** Accepted as written in `BUILD_SCOPE.md` §14.2. Copy into `docs/DECISIONS.md` in Phase 0. Highlights:
  - One Godot project builds client + dedicated server (feature tags + export presets).
  - Server-authoritative sim. Single-player is in-process `LocalAuthority` running the same `WorldSim`.
  - ENet + custom snapshots. No `MultiplayerSynchronizer` / `MultiplayerSpawner`.
  - 60 Hz sim, 20 Hz snapshots, client prediction for local movement only.
  - Players collide only with static terrain. Space queries for ropes/hits, not Area2D signals.
  - One World2D per MapInstance. Content is JSON + Schema via `index.json`.
  - Custom FastAPI + Postgres backend (not Nakama). HMAC join tickets. Item uids. One `CharacterRecord` shape.
  - Homelab Docker + Tailscale for alpha. Flat platforms only in MVP. Currency **Glimmer**. Classes Novice/Vanguard/Arcanist/Ranger/Shade.

## 2026-10-17 — Threat model (bootstrap)

- **Data:** accounts (later), character records, inventories/item uids, Glimmer, join tickets, chat (later). No payments. No real-money shop.
- **Boundaries:** Godot client → FastAPI (HTTPS/JWT); client → gameserver (ENet); gameserver → FastAPI `/internal/*` (service token); FastAPI → Postgres. Client must never call `/internal/*` or send positions/damage.
- **Attackers:** modified client, packet injector, credential stuffing (Phase 11+), stolen session, malicious dependency.
- **Blast radius:** one ticket/session = one character; service token = all character writes; DB = full persistence. Isolate keys. One active session per account.
- **Logging:** JSON lines on server. Never log passwords, JWTs, tickets, or HMAC secrets.
- **Recovery:** `save_version` + backups (Phase 16). Ticket TTL 30s, single-use. Tailscale-only until public profile.
- **Open risks:** homelab disk failure (R7); item dupe paths until Phase 11/12 tests exist; no public DDoS plan until Phase 16/17.

## 2026-08-29 — Vibe coder capability layer

- **Decision:** Golden path (`assets/stack-playbooks/golden-path.md`) is **opt-in** when the user has no stack preference — not an automatic default.
- **Why:** Speed for vibe coding without trapping users who named a stack.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Golden path as hard default; stay fully silent with no opinionated option.
- **Revisit when:** Most clones pick the same stack in practice.

- **Decision:** Feature integrations use one `add-integration` skill plus `assets/recipes/*.md`, not six nearly identical skills.
- **Why:** One procedure; stack/vendor detail stays on-demand; Cloud Agents get portable recipes without user-level vendor skills.
- **Alternatives rejected:** One skill per integration; relying only on `~/.cursor` vendor skills.
- **Revisit when:** A recipe grows large enough to need its own skill (migrations already did → `migrate-database`).

- **Decision:** UI polish is a `polish-ui` skill + `assets/checklists/ui-polish.md` (verifiable), with globbed `30-frontend.mdc` for local habits.
- **Why:** Vibe users judge on look/feel; always-apply must stay short.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Dumping a full style guide into always-apply rules.
- **Revisit when:** The product adopts a stricter design system.

## 2026-08-29 — Agent starter hardening

- **Decision:** Boilerplate (CI, GitHub templates, Docker, linters, hooks) stays under `assets/templates/` and is copied on demand — not materialized at repo root.
- **Why:** Keeps the starter stack-agnostic; Cloud and local clones stay blank until bootstrap.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Materializing CI/Docker at root; hybrid root+templates for every file.
- **Revisit when:** A preferred org-wide scanner replaces the local script. Skyrope CI is created in Phase 0 from BUILD_SCOPE §9.26, not from the Node template blindly.

- **Decision:** Security is both prose and tooling — `security-review` skill, `security-reviewer` subagent, `20-security.mdc`, checklists, `scripts/scan-secrets.mjs`, and a CI security-scan template.
- **Why:** Agents need a planned review path and a mechanical gate; Cloud Agents cannot rely on user-level security skills.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Checklist-only; tooling-only without a review runbook.
- **Revisit when:** A preferred org-wide scanner replaces the local script.

- **Decision:** Cursor hooks ship as inert templates under `assets/templates/hooks/` (Node `.mjs`), not enabled by default.
- **Why:** Hooks change every agent run; a bad deny rule blocks work. Node scripts are portable to Windows and Linux Cloud Agents (`.sh` is not).
- **Alternatives rejected:** Activating `.cursor/hooks.json` out of the box; shell-only hooks.
- **Revisit when:** The user asks to enable project hooks.

## Template defaults (2026-08-29)

- **Working memory lives in project rules**, not chat and not `~/.cursor`. Cloud Agents only see the repo.
- **Skills for workflows, rules for constraints.** Bootstrap, MCP, and memory updates are skills.
- **MCP is opt-in.** The catalog is in `assets/mcp-catalog.md`.
- **No application stack until bootstrap.** Skyrope is now the stack — see 2026-10-17 entries.

